.TH CLUSTER-COLLECT 1 "2026-09" "cluster-info-collector" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cluster-collect \- gather a Kubernetes incident support bundle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cluster-collect
.RI [ namespace ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects a support bundle from a live cluster \(em resources, describes,
events and container logs \(em and writes it as a tarball.
.PP
With no arguments it covers all namespaces. Configuration is by
environment variable rather than flags, so the same invocation works from
a shell, a Job manifest and a CI step.
.PP
Values that look like secrets are redacted from describe and resource
dumps by default.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NAMESPACES
Space-separated namespaces to collect (default: all namespaces).
.TP
.B LOG_TAIL_LINES
Log lines per container (default 2000).
.TP
.B INCLUDE_PREVIOUS
Also fetch previous-container logs (default true).
.TP
.B REDACT_ENV
Redact secret-like environment variable values (default true).
.TP
.B SINCE
Only fetch logs newer than this, e.g.
.BR 1h ,
.BR 30m
(default: all).
.TP
.B MAX_BUNDLE_MB
Truncate the biggest logs first past this size (default 0, unlimited).
.TP
.B OUTPUT_DIR
Where the tarball lands (default /tmp).
.TP
.B BUNDLE_S3_URI
Optional
.I s3://bucket/prefix
to upload the bundle to.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A bundle was written.
.TP
.B non-zero
The cluster could not be reached, or the bundle could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Everything, with an hour of logs:
.PP
.RS
.B SINCE=1h cluster-collect
.RE
.PP
Two namespaces, capped at 200 MB:
.PP
.RS
.B MAX_BUNDLE_MB=200 cluster-collect payments checkout
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/cluster-info-collector
